<h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>To Sum Up</strong> </h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The various microstructures of repo segments observed in the U.S. reflect how a heterogeneous set of participants evaluate the trade-offs involved in repo transactions differently. Costs related to the settlement of securities led to the emergence of tri-party repo; balance sheet costs favor central clearing; meanwhile, creative contracting—such as netted packages—mitigates costs in bilateral, non-centrally cleared repos.</p>



