<h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Summing Up</strong></h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Our preliminary analysis shows that trading activity concentrates in long-maturity principal STRIPS, aligning with the preferences of liability-driven investors such as pension funds and insurance companies for long-duration instruments. Principal STRIPS also tend to trade with higher prices than coupon STRIPS of the same maturity (as shown in &#8220;<a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/feds/using-treasury-strips-to-measure-the-yield-curve.htm">Using Treasury STRIPS to Measure the Yield Curve</a>,&#8221; for example). An interesting area for future analysis is the extent to which the higher trading volume of principal STRIPS is associated with higher liquidity and whether liquidity differences in the STRIPS market can help explain the pricing differences.</p>



