<h4 class="wp-block-heading">Watchpoints Abound</h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Because U.S. imports of both consumer electronics and AI-infrastructure components have shifted substantially into ASEAN, energy and petrochemical price shocks from the Strait of Hormuz disruption could pass through via higher input and transport costs and, in severe cases, physical shortages. For this reason, ASEAN energy vulnerabilities and specific product flows (laptops, memory, networking equipment and related components) bear close monitoring for anticipating potential near-term U.S. price and supply chain risks.</p>
</div></div>



