<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With the current energy price shock, a K-shaped pattern in gasoline consumption has opened up much more than before. Higher-income households have reduced real gas consumption only modestly and increased gasoline spending considerably compared with 2023. In contrast, lower-income households increased spending by much less and decreased real consumption by much more, potentially by carpooling or substituting to public transit where available. In subsequent releases of the EHIs, we will continue monitoring the consequences of the current energy price shock on different segments of our society.</p>



