<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Next, we examine in more detail the spending of high-income consumers. The chart below shows nominal and real retail spending cumulative growth for subdivisions of the $125,000+ income bracket. We see that for each of these brackets, retail sales relative to the January 2023 level are higher than for the bracket below it. The exception is the highest income bracket of households earning $250,000+, who, based on the CEX, spend a disproportionately large share of consumption (relative to the next highest bracket) on services that are aren’t comprehensively covered by Numerator, such as high-end restaurants, entertainment fees and admissions, education and insurance.</p>



<div style="height:15px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



